# tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf_witness.rish -- the shelf nothing wrote now has a writer.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf_witness.rish
#
# WHAT THIS GUARDS. Every send folds a ship's live-front account off `construction/ITINERARY.md`
# onto a shelf one directory deeper, so every relative link in the block must gain a level. The
# instrument that performs exactly that rewrite has existed since `20260826` and been general since
# `20260908.104232`, when its own header was widened to spell this very invocation. Measured
# `20260909`: 208 account shelves stand, all written by hand, and NOTHING under `tools/` writes one.
#
# THE FAULT IS NOT AN ABSENT TOOL; IT IS A TOOL NOTHING CALLS. `reds_fold.sh` pipes a REDS row
# through the filter, and that path has held. The account-shelf path has no writer at all, so the
# filter's use there depends on a hand recalling a pipe -- and the same day the header was widened,
# the fault fired again, from more than one ship. A prevention that is reachable and unknown fails
# the way an absent one does. The tree has ruled on this shape twice, at `%620` and at the row of
# `20260908.113404`: both end with the tool handing over what the hand kept mistyping.
#
# WHY THIS WRITER INVENTS A HEADER WHERE ITS REDS SIBLING REFUSES TO. `reds_fold.sh` refuses
# `shelf_absent` deliberately -- a REDS shelf's header names which rows moved and what they taught
# together, which is judgment. An account shelf's header names a seat and a stamp, both of them
# arguments, and one sentence that is the same every time. Nothing is judged here, so nothing is
# guessed. Measured across the 208 standing shelves, 34 share a first line and 12 share a body
# sentence, which is eight hands each writing the same header freshly -- reported rather than
# gated, since a differently worded header reads perfectly well.
#
# AND THE QUESTIONS THAT RIDE ALONG. A ship writes its ask for Keaton inside the account block --
# `**YOURS:** whether Tally seats a wake bound` -- and this writer moves the block whole, so the
# question leaves the live card by the same act that keeps the card under its bound. Measured
# `20260910`: **72** such asks stand across **54 of the 339** shelves, an account block's median
# life on the card is **104 minutes** with **283 of 292** lives under eight hours, and a grep for
# `**YOURS` under `tools/` returns one line of unrelated prose -- so nothing here reads a shelf for
# a question. From this stamp the writer prints every ask it shelves. The standing population is
# REPORTED below and gated at nothing, because answering an ask is Keaton's word and a guard that
# reddened on an unanswered question would red on ordinary work.

say "itinerary-account-shelf: Language EN -- the shelf that nothing wrote."
say "itinerary-account-shelf: Style Gauge, Meter -- the re-anchoring is done, never recalled."
say "itinerary-account-shelf: Lens TAME -- every refusal proven from both sides."

say "itinerary-account-shelf: the control -- the writer on a real fold in a throwaway pen..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/i/itinerary_account_shelf_control.sh"]
assert ctl.ok else "itinerary-account-shelf: the control refused --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"
assert ctl.out contains "pass=43 fail=0" else "itinerary-account-shelf: the control did not prove forty-three behaviors --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"

say "itinerary-account-shelf: the filter it delegates to must still stand..."
# invariant: the rewrite is computed in the filter and never duplicated here, so its absence is a
# refusal rather than a fallback -- one rule, one home.
let filt = run ["test" "-f" "tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold_reanchor.sh"]
assert filt.ok else "itinerary-account-shelf: tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold_reanchor.sh is absent -- the rewrite has no home"

say "itinerary-account-shelf: and the shelves standing in this tree read clean..."
# invariant: the writer exists to keep this reading at zero, so the guard states the property it
# serves rather than only proving its own machinery.
let depth = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -ohE '\\]\\(\\.\\./[a-z-]+/' construction/archive/*itinerary-landed-accounts.md 2>/dev/null | grep -cv '](../archive/' | sed 's/^/pin_depth_links=/'"]
assert depth.ok else "itinerary-account-shelf: the shelf reading refused --\n${depth.err}"
assert depth.out contains "pin_depth_links=0" else "itinerary-account-shelf: an account shelf carries a pin-depth link --\n${depth.out}"

say "itinerary-account-shelf: and the questions already shelved, counted so the number is readable..."
# invariant: reported and never gated -- the count rises whenever a ship asks something, which is
# ordinary work, and only Keaton's word lowers it.
let asks = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -hoE '[*][*]YOURS' construction/archive/*itinerary-landed-accounts.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ' | sed 's/^/asks_shelved_standing=/'"]
assert asks.ok else "itinerary-account-shelf: the ask reading refused --\n${asks.err}"
say "itinerary-account-shelf: ${asks.out}"

say "itinerary-account-shelf: GREEN -- 43 behaviors, the filter in place, the shelves clean, the second run asked of the bytes, and every ask the writer shelves now said out loud."
